---
description: Writing database migrations
globs: db/migrations/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- `db/migrate.ts` records applied filenames only (no checksum), so editing
  an applied migration silently does nothing on existing databases. Never
  edit one; add the next numbered file (`NNNN_snake_case.sql`).
- Migrations must be safe to run on the live database: `IF NOT EXISTS`,
  backfills that are idempotent, no destructive rewrites of paid history.
  When a migration fixes existing data, keep the old rows somewhere finance
  can review (see 0077's `_duplicates` table) and say so in `BUGS.md`.
- Money columns are `BIGINT`. `ledger_entries` stays append-only.
- After adding one: `npm run migrate` against the test DB, then both suites.
